From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shupeng Xue <dspxue@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:11:23 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] wifi: b43: HT-PHY: don't flag coding rate 2/3 in PHY
 control word 1

With B43_TXH_PHY1_CRATE_2_3 set, the HT-PHY transmits frames that no
receiver decodes, and reports no error. Among legacy rates this bit is
only used for 48 Mbit/s, as in brcmsmac's legacy_phycfg_table for the
N-PHY. On a BCM4331 at 2.4 GHz, a monitor next to it decoded none of
the ~2500 frames minstrel tried at 48 Mbit/s in 40 seconds, while it
did decode 54 Mbit/s ones; with the bit cleared it decoded 124. Rate
control never learns to avoid the rate: the retransmissions at the
fallback rate succeed, and minstrel keeps crediting 48 Mbit/s with
about 30% success.

The problem is the bit, not the rate: with HT rates (not supported by
b43 yet), setting it as brcmsmac's mcs_table does for the coding rate
2/3 MCSs makes MCS 5 and 13 fail the same way. Sweeping the coding
rate field shows the HT-PHY takes the rate from the PLCP header: any
even value transmits correct frames, any odd value fails. Clear the bit
on HT-PHY only.

Assisted-by: pi:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/xmit.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/xmit.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/xmit.c
index f0b082596637..4de6e5042c55 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/xmit.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/xmit.c
@@ -186,6 +186,11 @@ static u16 b43_generate_tx_phy_ctl1(struct b43_wldev *dev, u8 bitrate)
 			control |= e->coding_rate;
 			control |= e->modulation;
 		}
+		/* The HT-PHY takes the coding rate from the PLCP header;
+		 * with this bit set it sends frames nobody can decode.
+		 */
+		if (phy->type == B43_PHYTYPE_HT)
+			control &= ~B43_TXH_PHY1_CRATE_2_3;
 		control |= B43_TXH_PHY1_MODE_SISO;
 	}
 
